WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:01.617
- [Steve] The anechoic chamber

00:00:01.617 --> 00:00:05.559
is a test lab for doing acoustic testing.

00:00:05.559 --> 00:00:09.642
It's a chamber within a
chamber within a chamber.

00:00:12.008 --> 00:00:13.120
- [Woman] That's Steve.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:14.975
- [Steve] I'm Steve
Orfield, the founder of

00:00:14.975 --> 00:00:17.850
Orfield Laboratories in Minneapolis.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.046
- [Woman] And we're talking
about what it feels like

00:00:20.046 --> 00:00:23.796
to sit in one of the
quietest rooms on earth.

00:00:25.758 --> 00:00:29.653
An anechoic chamber is a
room that absorbs sound.

00:00:29.653 --> 00:00:31.104
So, it's quiet.

00:00:31.104 --> 00:00:33.845
- [Steve] When we put subjects
in the anechoic chamber,

00:00:33.845 --> 00:00:37.176
we sit them in a chair,
and we turn off the lights.

00:00:37.176 --> 00:00:39.384
- [Woman] It turns out
that the only noises

00:00:39.384 --> 00:00:40.934
you'd hear in there are noises

00:00:40.934 --> 00:00:44.024
that come from inside your own body.

00:00:44.024 --> 00:00:45.957
- [Steve] Right away, you'll usually hear

00:00:45.957 --> 00:00:48.540
the sound of your ears buzzing.

00:00:49.458 --> 00:00:50.812
You'll start to hear the joints

00:00:50.812 --> 00:00:53.418
in your arms and in your legs,

00:00:53.418 --> 00:00:56.801
like the sound of rubbing
two pieces of wood together.

00:00:56.801 --> 00:01:00.248
(wood grinding)

00:01:00.248 --> 00:01:02.403
You'll clearly hear your heart beating.

00:01:02.403 --> 00:01:06.236
Kind of a boom, boom, boom, boom, boom.

00:01:06.236 --> 00:01:08.269
(heart thumping)

00:01:08.269 --> 00:01:10.168
The flow of the air into your lungs.

00:01:10.168 --> 00:01:13.437
(lungs inhaling and exhaling)

00:01:13.437 --> 00:01:15.185
- [Woman] And sounds from inside your body

00:01:15.185 --> 00:01:17.780
that you might've heard
outside the chamber

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:20.059
are suddenly so much louder.

00:01:20.059 --> 00:01:21.517
- [Steve] Any noise
that would be startling

00:01:21.517 --> 00:01:22.911
outside the chamber would be

00:01:22.911 --> 00:01:25.620
16 times as startling inside the chamber.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.828
- [Woman] Noises like
your stomach growling,

00:01:27.828 --> 00:01:29.593
(thunderous growling)

00:01:29.593 --> 00:01:30.801
or your knuckles cracking.

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:32.281
(knuckles cracking and popping)

00:01:32.281 --> 00:01:35.280
People don't last that long inside.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:37.103
- [Steve] Maybe an hour and 15 minutes.

00:01:37.103 --> 00:01:41.073
- [Woman] And that's mainly
because of one of two reasons.

00:01:41.073 --> 00:01:44.283
- [Steve] Some people
find that very relaxing.

00:01:44.283 --> 00:01:48.639
Some people find that
fearful or claustrophobic.

00:01:48.639 --> 00:01:50.668
- [Woman] One person's peace and quiet

00:01:50.668 --> 00:01:53.685
is another's personal nightmare.

00:01:53.685 --> 00:01:56.518
(whimsical music)

